TITLE:: SDGBusTrack
summary:: what a return and the master share: a chain of effects, sends, a fader, mute, solo and an output
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SDGReturn, Classes/SDGMaster, Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGInsert

DESCRIPTION::
A track of the mixer that is not an orbit. Audio comes in on a bus, runs through a
chain of effects - link::Classes/SDGInsert::s, the same objects as on an orbit: eq,
compressor, insight, an sc fx kit effect, a VST plugin - then sends to the returns, a
fader with mute and solo, a meter, and out: to the master, or straight to a hardware bus.

code::
a = ~sdg.addReturn;                       // return A
~sdg.addBusInsert(a, \compressor);
a.level = 0.8;
a.route(\direct, 2);                      // the return to hardware 2-3, past the master
a.route(\master);                         // back
::

subsection:: Where it runs

Nothing of it is in an orbit. Its synths run in the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-returnGroup::
after SuperDirt's group, in the order the signal takes: the returns' heads, the
returns, the master. The master's effects work in place on its in bus, since
everything that writes to it has run by then.

subsection:: Who owns what

The link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: makes and frees them. No event reaches a bus track, so
an effect's own sleep would cut its tail: a tick once a second resumes its effects, and
it is always on, as in a DAW. After a cmd-period everything comes back with its levels,
a VST plugin with the state it last read back. A link::Classes/SDGSession:: saves them.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: shortName
RETURNS:: what a person calls it, and the window's name for its strip.

METHOD:: inserts
RETURNS:: its chain, link::Classes/SDGInsert::s in signal order.

METHOD:: level
The fader, an amplitude from 0 to 4.
ARGUMENT:: amp
the amplitude.

METHOD:: muted
RETURNS:: whether it is muted. Set it with link::#-mute::.

METHOD:: mute
Mute it, and what it sends.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: soloed
RETURNS:: whether it is soloed. Set it with link::#-solo::.

METHOD:: solo
Solo it: see link::Classes/SDGReturn#Rules for sends::.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: preFader
On a return: whether what is sent into it is taken before the source's fader.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: limitertype
The output's guard: 0 nothing, 1 a limiter, 2 a soft clip.
ARGUMENT:: value
the number.

METHOD:: route
Where it goes. Nothing restarts.
ARGUMENT:: argDest
code::\master:: or code::\direct::.
ARGUMENT:: bus
for code::\direct::, the hardware bus; nil keeps the one it had.

METHOD:: dest
RETURNS:: code::\master:: or code::\direct::.

METHOD:: directBus
RETURNS:: the hardware bus it writes to when it goes direct.

METHOD:: outBus
The bus it writes to now. Setting it sends it direct to that bus.
ARGUMENT:: index
a bus number, or a link::Classes/Bus::.

METHOD:: returnLevel
ARGUMENT:: target
an link::Classes/SDGReturn::.
RETURNS:: the level of the send to it, 0 to 1.

METHOD:: targets
RETURNS:: the returns it sends to.

METHOD:: inBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: that comes in.

METHOD:: lineBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: its effects work on.

METHOD:: tapBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: holding what it plays, after its fader: what the recorder reads.

METHOD:: nodes
RETURNS:: its synths in signal order.

METHOD:: metering
Whether it sends its levels as code::'/sdgtrack'::, 20 a second. The window turns this on.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.
